		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>ResolutionWidth</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1360</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
			<Hint>Window size (fullscreen: the display mode). 1360 x 768 is the arcade resolution. Above it the game keeps running at 1360x768 and TeknoParrot scales the whole picture (ResolutionMode Upscale), so every menu, story talk box, ticker and HUD element stays in place. Any size up to 3840 x 2160 (4K) and beyond; use 16:9 sizes (1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3840x2160). Windows larger than the desktop are allowed.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>ResolutionHeight</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>768</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
			<Hint>See ResolutionWidth. 768 = the arcade resolution.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>ResolutionMode</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>Upscale</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>Upscale</string>
				<string>Game</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>Upscale (recommended): the game runs at its native 1360x768 and the picture is scaled to ResolutionWidth x ResolutionHeight; all 2D elements stay where they belong. Game: the old behaviour, the game's own resolution code runs at that size (above 1360x768 some menus, story talk boxes and ticker clips are misplaced).</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>RenderResolution</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>Auto</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>Auto</string>
				<string>Stock</string>
				<string>1.5x</string>
				<string>2x</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>3D scene resolution when the output is above 1360x768 (Upscale). Auto: at least the output size (1:1 sharp 3D). Stock: the renderer.ini of the game (ID6 / ID7 962x768, ID8 1443x1152). 1.5x / 2x: that multiple of the output (supersampling, more GPU load).</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
