		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Show settings</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>Basic</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>Basic</string>
				<string>Advanced</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>Initial D starts online by default: at every start TeknoParrot checks the online server, and with this PC registered (Account page) you get nationwide matchmaking, events and rankings. Without registration, or when the server cannot be reached, the game starts offline within seconds. Basic: nothing to set. Advanced: online server, LAN group and peers, seat, cabinet serial, the cabinet's EEPROM network record.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>NetworkMode</FieldName>
			<VisibleWhen>Show settings</VisibleWhen>
			<VisibleWhenValue>Debug</VisibleWhenValue>
			<FieldValue>Auto</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>Auto</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>TPUI always selects Auto. Online when the server answers and this PC is registered; otherwise offline or LAN.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Ip</FieldName>
			<VisibleWhen>Show settings</VisibleWhen>
